 We start by expanding the expression inside the square root:
\begin{align*}
g(x) &= \sqrt{(x-3)^2-(x-8)^2} \\
&= \sqrt{(x^2 - 6x + 9) - (x^2 - 16x + 64)} \\
&= \sqrt{x^2 - 6x + 9 - x^2 + 16x - 64} \\
&= \sqrt{10x - 55}.
\end{align*}
Since the expression inside the square root must be nonnegative, we have $10x - 55 \ge 0$, which implies $x \ge \frac{55}{10} = \boxed{\frac{11}{2}}$.
The answer is: \frac{11}{2}

